id: 36
hanzi: 海里
pinyin: hǎi lǐ
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Measure Word

meanings_summary:
  en: nautical mile; sea mile (unit of maritime distance, approx. 1,852 meters)
  es: milla náutica; milla marina (unidad de distancia marina, aprox. 1.852 metros)

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Measure Word | Standard | unit of distance used in maritime and aerial navigation, equal to 1,852 meters | unidad de distancia usada en navegación marítima y aérea (1.852 m) | 航行五十海里 (sail fifty nautical miles)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 帆船以平均六节的航速日夜前行，全家人在两个月内顺利完成了上千海里的远洋航程。 | Fānchuán yǐ píngjūn liù jié de hángsù rìyè qiánxíng, quán jiārén zài liǎng gè yuè nèi shùnlì wánchéng le shàng qiān hǎilǐ de yuǎnyáng hángchéng. | The sailboat advanced day and night at an average speed of six knots, completing over a thousand nautical miles within two months. | El velero navegó día y noche a una media de seis nudos, completando con éxito más de mil millas náuticas en dos meses.
  #2 | 海事搜救直升机飞赴距海岸线两百海里的外海区域，成功营救出遇险货轮上的受困船员。 | Hǎishì sōujiù zhíshēngjī fēifù jù hǎi'ànxiàn liǎng bǎi hǎilǐ de wàihǎi qūyù, chénggōng yíngjiù chū yùxiǎn huòlún shàng de shòukùn chuányuán. | The maritime rescue helicopter flew 200 nautical miles offshore, successfully rescuing stranded crew members from the distressed freighter. | El helicóptero de salvamento marítimo voló a doscientas millas náuticas mar adentro para rescatar a los marineros de un mercante en apuros.

